Base commit: 9137b00fe4c250029e043d4cf9b7f556f72ee9a2

Built with `nix build .#cloud-redirect` under `pkgs.pkgsi686Linux.stdenv`
(genuine i686 toolchain, not -m32 cross-compilation on a 64-bit compiler --
see nix-modules/default.nix). This sidesteps CMakeLists.txt's Fedora/Debian
multilib-path guessing for LINUX_32BIT entirely, since CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P is
already 4 under that stdenv.

Confirmed ELF32/Intel 80386. NEEDED: libdl.so.2, libpthread.so.0,
libatomic.so.1, libstdc++.so.6, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6 -- no
unexpected dependencies (CloudRedirect's Linux target needs no openssl/curl,
unlike its Windows target).

test/linux_lua_discovery_tests and test/linux_init_stop_tests (the two tests
this port added) both pass, built as native 64-bit binaries since both only
exercise header-only, ABI-independent logic (lua_discovery.h, init_stop.h).
The rest of test/*.cpp has not been run this pass.

Built via `make ronin-module` (nix build .#cloud-redirect + stage into
module/payload/), the same target `make deploy-tsuki-module` and
`make rollback-tsuki-module` depend on.

Packaged artifacts:

e3d9e89ff95b0a83b3de6367e1959d06aa4a49b30ce25f87c50d94edd9223455  payload/cloud_redirect.so

`ronin_validate.py` from ronin-module-sdk passes clean (zero failures) as
of this revision. The runtime-evidence gap noted in earlier revisions of
this file is closed: `interface.json` declares the `cloud-hook` component's
health readiness as `runtime-evidence` with carrier `runtime-file`, and
`src/platform/linux/init.cpp`'s `PublishRoninEvidence()` writes the backing
record (`observed_at`, `process_instance`, `status`) to
`$TSUKI_RONIN_RUNTIME_DIR_CLOUDREDIRECT/ready.json` once hooks are
confirmed installed. This required a small addition to Tsuki itself
(`lua/roninmodule.lua` gained a `runtime-file` evidence reader; it
previously only understood `companion-export`, which this
companion-less package can't use). Verified end to end: `make
deploy-tsuki-module` actually installs into a real Tsuki checkout, and
that checkout's own `tools/test_cloudredirect_manifest.lua` passes 6/6
against the installed package.
